
---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout path="/privacy/" title="Privacy Policy" description="WheelCanvas privacy practices: browser-local random selection, optional local storage, link sharing and future advertising disclosures.">
<section class="hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Our policies</span><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p>Updated November 11, 2026</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container article">
  <h2>How the wheel handles your entries</h2>
  <p>Wheel entries, number exclusions and draws are processed in your browser. The core app does not send the list to a WheelCanvas server and does not require user accounts.</p>
  <h3>Optional local saving</h3>
  <p>When you select “Save locally,” the configuration is stored in localStorage on your device. You can clear the saved data using “Clear saved” or your browser controls. We do not currently use a backend database.</p>
  <h3>Shareable links</h3>
  <p>The Share setup action encodes the configuration into the URL fragment. Anyone you give that URL to can read its contents; do not include private names or other sensitive information. URLs may be retained in browser history or copied elsewhere.</p>
  <h3>Hosting and technical logs</h3>
  <p>The site is intended to be served over Cloudflare Pages. Hosting and CDN providers may process technical requests including IP addresses as necessary to serve the website and maintain security. Their handling is subject to their own policies.</p>
  <h3>Advertising and analytics</h3>
  <p>No advertising or analytics tracking script is included in this release. If advertising is enabled later, this page and any necessary consent mechanisms will be updated before such scripts are added.</p>
  <h3>Contact</h3><p>For questions or corrections, use the public project's <a href="https://github.com/garrison2025/Random-Wheel/issues">GitHub issue tracker</a>. Please do not post sensitive personal information in a public issue.</p>
</div></section>
</BaseLayout>
